---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CallToAction from "../components/CallToAction.astro";
import ContactCTA from "../components/ContactCTA.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Sathiyaraman M | Solution Consultant & Engineer"
	description="Sathiyaraman M is a Solution Consultant and Engineer at Sahaj Software, working across technical consulting, software engineering, and platform engineering."
>
	<div class="stack gap-20 lg:gap-48">
		<main class="wrapper stack gap-20 lg:gap-32">
			<header class="hero-section">
				<Hero title="Hello, I’m Sathiyaraman." tagline="I’m a Solution Consultant and Engineer at Sahaj Software. I work across consulting, software engineering, and platform engineering to make complex problems easier to solve." align="start">
					<div class="hero-actions">
						<CallToAction href="#about">A little about me <Icon icon="arrow-right" size="1.1em" /></CallToAction>
						<a class="text-link" href="/Sathiyaraman M's Resume.pdf" target="_blank">View my resume</a>
					</div>
				</Hero>
				<img class="hero-image" alt="Sathiyaraman M" width="480" height="620" src="/assets/portrait.jpeg" />
			</header>

			<section class="intro" id="about">
				<p class="eyebrow">A short version</p>
				<h2>I like understanding the whole problem before writing the first line of code.</h2>
				<div class="intro-copy">
					<p>My work sits between people, systems, and code. I help turn unclear problems into practical technical direction, then stay close enough to the implementation to make sure the solution works in the real world.</p>
					<p>I bring a strong .NET and C# foundation from years of building software, along with current experience in the JVM ecosystem, TypeScript, Node.js, React, and platform engineering. The technology matters, but choosing what is useful, understandable, and maintainable matters more.</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="timeline-section" aria-labelledby="journey-title">
				<div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The journey so far</p><h2 id="journey-title">From building software to helping shape how it gets built.</h2></div>
				<ol class="timeline">
					<li><span class="timeline-marker">01</span><div><h3>A .NET foundation</h3><p>My early years in software were shaped by .NET, C#, ASP.NET Core, Blazor, and SQL Server. That foundation is still a core part of how I think and build.</p></div></li>
					<li><span class="timeline-marker">02</span><div><h3>Learning by making</h3><p>Projects, hackathons, and hands-on experimentation taught me to connect technical decisions with the people and problems behind them.</p></div></li>
					<li><span class="timeline-marker">03</span><div><h3>Consulting and engineering at Sahaj</h3><p>For the past two years, I’ve worked across technical consulting, decision-making, implementation, and platform engineering.</p></div></li>
					<li><span class="timeline-marker">04</span><div><h3>What I’m focused on now</h3><p>Today, I work mostly with JVM technologies and the TypeScript ecosystem, including Node.js and React, while continuing to bring my .NET experience to the problems I solve.</p></div></li>
				</ol>
			</section>

			<section class="perspective" aria-labelledby="perspective-title">
				<p class="eyebrow">How I approach work</p>
				<h2 id="perspective-title">Clear thinking, useful technology, and enough curiosity to keep learning.</h2>
				<div class="principles">
					<div><h3>Start with the problem</h3><p>Good solutions begin with listening carefully and understanding what success actually means.</p></div>
					<div><h3>Keep the system understandable</h3><p>Complexity is sometimes necessary, but it should never be the default or the selling point.</p></div>
					<div><h3>Stay close to the work</h3><p>I enjoy the conversation around architecture just as much as the craft of implementing it.</p></div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="closing-note"><p>There is more to me than a list of technologies. I write occasionally, keep learning, and make things when an idea is interesting enough to follow.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://blogs.sathiyaraman-m.com/" target="_blank">Read what I write <Icon icon="arrow-right" size="1em" /></a></section>
		</main>
		<ContactCTA />
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.hero-section { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 2rem; }
	.hero-image { aspect-ratio: 5 / 4; object-fit: cover; object-position: top; border-radius: 1.5rem; box-shadow: var(--shadow-md); }
	.hero-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 1.25rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
	.text-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; color: var(--gray-200); text-underline-offset: 0.25em; text-decoration-color: var(--gray-600); transition: color var(--theme-transition), text-decoration-color var(--theme-transition); }
	.text-link:hover, .text-link:focus { color: var(--gray-0); text-decoration-color: currentColor; }
	.intro, .timeline-section, .perspective, .closing-note { max-width: 65ch; margin-inline: auto; width: 100%; }
	.eyebrow { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; color: var(--accent-regular); font-family: var(--font-brand); font-size: var(--text-sm); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
	.intro h2, .perspective h2, .section-heading h2 { font-size: var(--text-2xl); color: var(--gray-0); }
	.intro-copy { display: grid; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; color: var(--gray-300); font-size: var(--text-lg); }
	.timeline-section { max-width: 75ch; }
	.section-heading { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
	.timeline { display: grid; gap: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
	.timeline li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 3.5rem 1fr; gap: 1rem; position: relative; padding-bottom: 2.5rem; }
	.timeline li:not(:last-child)::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 1.05rem; top: 2rem; bottom: 0; width: 1px; background: var(--gray-700); }
	.timeline-marker { z-index: 1; display: grid; place-items: center; width: 2.1rem; height: 2.1rem; border: 1px solid var(--accent-regular); border-radius: 50%; color: var(--accent-regular); background: var(--gray-999); font-family: var(--font-brand); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
	.timeline h3, .principles h3 { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: var(--gray-0); font-size: var(--text-lg); }
	.timeline p, .principles p { color: var(--gray-400); }
	.perspective { max-width: 75ch; padding: 2rem; border: 1px solid var(--gray-800); border-radius: 1.5rem; background: var(--gray-999_40); }
	.principles { display: grid; gap: 1.5rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
	.closing-note { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; color: var(--gray-300); }
	@media (min-width: 50em) {
		.hero-section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 6fr 4fr; gap: 3.75rem; align-items: center; }
		.hero-image { aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; border-radius: 4.5rem; }
		.intro h2, .perspective h2, .section-heading h2 { font-size: var(--text-3xl); }
		.intro-copy { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; }
		.principles { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 2rem; }
		.perspective { padding: 3rem; }
	}
</style>
